1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Plan three healthy dinners for four people
with a €40 target, using Picnic deals where possible.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Picnic is named in the request, so ChatGPT
looks up its current deals through KortingZoeker.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The app uses get_current_discounts for Picnic.
No category filter keeps all deal categories available.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:32,000
ChatGPT uses the available deals
to build a meal plan around the budget.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The plan brings together meal ideas,
shared ingredients and a combined grocery list.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The estimated total is €37.63 —
within the €40 target for three dinners for four.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Dinner ideas include salmon with potatoes and spinach,
and courgette bolognese pasta.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
A pumpkin, chickpea and minced-meat chili completes the plan.
Shared ingredients help make the budget go further.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
One combined shopping list separates
€27.53 in deal-backed prices from other groceries.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Other groceries add an estimated €10.10.
Final prices and availability may vary.

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:23,000
What happens if you ask the app
to order the groceries and pay at Picnic?

12
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,000
KortingZoeker provides deals for planning.
It cannot place orders or process payments.

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,325
Complete checkout at the retailer.
Purchases remain under your control.
